Registry-Based E2E Testing System for Unified Platform
Core Concept
A centralized registry stores all definitions (Entities, Components, Templates, Layouts, Intents, Operations) as versioned schemas. An E2E testing flow automatically validates every combination and interaction path using these registry entries.

HIGH-LEVEL SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    UNIFIED PLATFORM                             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                 │
│  ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐   │
│  │  DEFINITION   │     │   REGISTRY   │     │   TEST       │   │
│  │  AUTHORING   │────▶│   STORE      │────▶│  ORCHESTRATOR│   │
│  │  (UI Forms)  │     │  (Versioned) │     │              │   │
│  └──────────────┘     └──────────────┘     └──────────────┘   │
│                                                    │           │
│                              ┌─────────────────────┘           │
│                              ▼                                 │
│  ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐   │
│  │  TEST        │     │  FLOW        │     │  REPORT      │   │
│  │  GENERATOR  │────▶│  EXECUTOR    │────▶│  AGGREGATOR  │   │
│  │  (Combinator)│    │  (Parallel)  │     │  (Pass/Fail) │   │
│  └──────────────┘     └──────────────┘     └──────────────┘   │
│                                                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
REGISTRY STRUCTURE
Registry Table	Stores	Key Metadata
Entity Registry	All 17 Entity Types	Schema, validators, parent relationships
Component Registry	All 35+ Components	Render props, events, dependencies
Template Registry	All 25+ Templates	Pre-configured entity-component combos
Layout Registry	All 15+ Layouts	Container rules, responsive breakpoints
Intent Registry	All 25+ Intents	Triggers, success criteria, user flows
Operation Registry	All 50+ Operations	Input schemas, output schemas, side effects
Validation Registry	Cross-entity rules	Which operations work on which entities
State Registry	System states	Pre-conditions, post-conditions for each operation
TEST GENERATION FLOW
Step 1: Registry Crawling
Pull all definitions from registry tables

Map relationships: Which Operations apply to which Entities

Identify paths: Operation sequence that fulfills each Intent

Step 2: Combinatorial Test Generation
text
For each Intent:
  1. Get required Operations
  2. Get applicable Entities
  3. Get compatible Components
  4. Generate permutations:
     - Entity A → Operation X → Entity B
     - Component Y + Layout Z rendering Entity A
     - Template T instantiated with all Operation combos
Step 3: Test Case Assembly
Test Type	Generated From	Example
CRUD Tests	Entity + Create/Read/Update/Delete Ops	Create Document → Update Content → Delete
Workflow Tests	Node + Edge + Execute Operation	Trigger → Action → Filter → Sink
UI Tests	Component + Layout + Render Op	Render Dashboard with 2x2 Grid
Integration Tests	Template + All Ops	Instantiate ETL Template → Run → Export
State Transition Tests	Intent + Operation Sequence	Analyze Intent → Run Cell → Visualize
Error Tests	Operation + Invalid Input	Execute Workflow with missing Credential
Permission Tests	User Role + Operation	Viewer tries to Delete Entity
Step 4: Test Prioritization
P0: Core CRUD + Render (all Entities/Components)

P1: Most used Templates + Intents

P2: Edge cases, error handling, permissions

P3: Cross-entity complex flows

E2E TEST EXECUTION PIPELINE
text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   TEST PIPELINE                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                         │
│  1. SETUP PHASE                                         │
│     └─ Spin isolated test workspace                     │
│     └─ Seed registry definitions                        │
│     └─ Initialize test user with all roles             │
│                                                         │
│  2. EXECUTION PHASE  (Parallel)                        │
│     ├─ Group A: Entity Operations (CRUD all types)     │
│     ├─ Group B: Workflow Operations (n8n flows)        │
│     ├─ Group C: Notebook Operations (Jupyter)          │
│     ├─ Group D: UI Rendering (all Components/Layouts)  │
│     ├─ Group E: Template Instantiation (all templates) │
│     └─ Group F: Cross-domain flows (Intent sequences)  │
│                                                         │
│  3. VALIDATION PHASE                                    │
│     ├─ Assert expected output schema                   │
│     ├─ Assert UI renders without errors               │
│     ├─ Assert state changes (Registry's state table)   │
│     ├─ Assert error messages for negative tests        │
│     └─ Assert no side effects in isolated workspace   │
│                                                         │
│  4. TEARDOWN PHASE                                      │
│     └─ Clean test workspace                            │
│     └─ Archive test run logs                           │
│                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
COVERAGE MATRIX (What Gets Tested)
Coverage Dimension	Scope	Count
Entity Coverage	All 17 entity types × CRUD operations	~68 tests
Component Coverage	All 35 components × render in all layouts	~525 tests
Template Coverage	All 25 templates × instantiation + default ops	~25+ tests
Intent Coverage	All 25 intents × success path operations	~25 tests
Operation Coverage	All 50+ ops × valid input + invalid input	~100+ tests
Cross-Coverage	Entity A → Operation X → Entity B (valid combos from registry)	Dynamic (1000+)
Flow Coverage	End-to-end user journeys (Intent sequences)	~50 flows
Error Coverage	All error types (network, validation, auth, timeout)	~30 tests
Permission Coverage	All roles × all operations on all entities	~200+ tests
ORCHESTRATOR COMPONENTS
Component	Responsibility
Test Generator	Reads registry → generates JSON test definitions
Test Scheduler	Queues tests based on priority, dependencies, parallelism
Test Runner	Executes tests against isolated platform instance
Assertion Engine	Compares actual vs expected using registry schemas
State Tracker	Records before/after states for each test
Flaky Detector	Re-runs failed tests to identify intermittent failures
Report Aggregator	Collects pass/fail, time, coverage percentages
Regression Detector	Compares with baseline (previous registry version)
FEEDBACK LOOP
text
Registry Update → Test Generation → E2E Execution → Report → 
    ↓                                                    ↓
[PASS] ──────▶ Merge registry update                     
[FAIL] ──────▶ Block merge ──▶ Alert team ──▶ Fix registry or platform
Commit Hook: Registry changes trigger test generation automatically

Daily Cron: Full regression suite runs on production-like environment

On-Demand: Developers can run subset tests during development

REPORTING & MONITORING
Report Type	Content	Purpose
Test Run Summary	Pass/Fail %, time, flaky count	Quick health check
Coverage Report	% Entities/Components/Templates/Intents/Ops tested	Gaps identification
Performance Report	Operation latency percentiles	Performance regression
Error Heatmap	Which entities/ops fail most	Prioritization for fixes
Registry Drift Report	What changed since last test	Impact analysis
Compatibility Matrix	Which operations work with which entities	Documentation & discovery
KEY PRINCIPLES
Principle	Implementation
Self-Testing	The platform tests itself using its own registry
Declarative Tests	Tests are generated from registry, not hand-coded
Version Awareness	Registry versions map to platform versions
Isolation	Each test run has fresh, clean workspace
Parallelism	Independent tests run simultaneously to save time
Determinism	Random seeds for data generation ensure reproducibility
Traceability	Each failure links back to registry entry and operation
Continuous	Runs on every registry change, every commit
EXAMPLE TEST GENERATION (High-Level)
From Registry:

Entity: Workflow (has Nodes + Edges)

Operation: Execute Workflow (requires valid Nodes + Credentials)

Intent: Automate (success criteria: output matches expected)

Component: Flowchart Plane (renders Nodes + Edges)

Generated Tests:

Create Workflow → Add Node (Trigger) → Add Node (Action) → Connect → Execute → Validate Output

Create Workflow → Delete Node → Execute → Validate Error

Create Workflow → Render in Flowchart Plane → Assert all Nodes visible

Create Workflow → Save as Template → Instantiate → Execute → Compare results

Create Workflow → Add invalid Credential → Execute → Assert specific error message

Viewer role tries to Execute → Assert permission denied

All tests run automatically, no manual coding, fully covered by registry definitions.

CONCLUSION
This system ensures 100% coverage of all definitions in your registry without writing a single test script. The registry acts as the single source of truth for both the platform functionality and its test cases, creating a self-validating ecosystem where any change to Entities, Components, Templates, Layouts, Intents, or Operations automatically triggers the right tests.

